Design a complete modern mobile application UI/UX for an AI-powered student career guidance platform called **“Kareer.ai”**.

Kareer.ai helps students discover suitable educational fields and potential careers through adaptive AI assessments, personalized recommendations, career roadmaps, educational content, videos, news, analytics, and interview preparation.

The application must feel like a combination of:

* A modern AI application
* A premium education platform
* A career discovery application
* A personalized recommendation platform

Do NOT make it look like a generic chatbot.

## BRAND & VISUAL THEME

Use a consistent visual identity throughout the application.

Primary visual direction:

* Deep navy / indigo as the main brand color
* Electric blue and subtle violet as accent colors
* White/light backgrounds for most content
* Soft blue/purple gradients for important AI elements
* Dark navy sections where appropriate
* Rounded cards and modern spacing
* Clean, minimal, premium interface
* Subtle shadows
* Soft gradient backgrounds
* Modern line icons
* Inter or Poppins typography
* Large readable headings
* Accessible contrast
* Friendly but professional design

The application has TWO dashboard experiences:

### JUNIOR DASHBOARD

For students in Grade 7–10.

The junior interface should be:

* Friendly
* Colorful but not childish
* More visual
* Rounded
* Encouraging
* Easy to understand
* Suitable for teenagers

Use illustrations, friendly icons, progress indicators, badges and simple language.

### SENIOR DASHBOARD

For students in Grade 11, Grade 12 and BS/university.

The senior interface should be:

* More professional
* Analytical
* Career-focused
* Modern
* Data-driven
* Slightly more sophisticated

Use charts, analytics cards, career match percentages, timelines, graphs and professional icons.

Both dashboards must maintain the same Kareer.ai brand identity.

---

# SCREEN 1 — SPLASH SCREEN

Create a premium splash screen.

Include:

* Kareer.ai logo
* AI-inspired career/compass/path icon
* Tagline:

“Discover Your Path. Build Your Future.”

Use a subtle blue/purple gradient background.

---

# SCREEN 2 — LOGIN

Create a clean login screen.

Include:

* Kareer.ai logo
* Welcome message
* Email field
* Password field
* Forgot password
* Login button
* Google login option
* Link to Sign Up

Keep the design minimal.

---

# SCREEN 3 — SIGN UP

Include:

* Full name
* Email
* Password
* Confirm password
* Create account button
* Google signup
* Login link

---

# SCREEN 4 — INITIAL PROFILE SETUP

After signup, students answer initial questions that personalize the application.

Create a multi-step onboarding flow.

Questions should include:

1. What is your current education level?
2. What subjects do you enjoy?
3. What activities interest you?
4. What are your hobbies?
5. What type of work do you enjoy?
6. Do you already have a career in mind?

Use:

* Progress indicator
* One question per screen
* Large selectable cards
* Icons
* Friendly explanations
* Continue button

The education level determines which dashboard the student receives.

---

# SCREEN 5 — EDUCATION LEVEL SELECTION

Create a visual selection screen containing:

Grade 7
Grade 8
Grade 9
Grade 10
Grade 11
Grade 12
BS / University

After selection, explain:

“Your answers will help Kareer.ai personalize your career journey.”

---

# JUNIOR EXPERIENCE — GRADE 7–10

Create a dedicated Junior Dashboard.

Header:
“Good morning, Alex 👋”

Subtitle:
“Let’s discover what could be right for you.”

Main hero card:

“Ready to discover your path?”

Button:
“Start Assessment”

Show assessment progress.

For students who have already completed Session 1, replace the button with:

“Start Session 2”

After each completed session, dynamically change it to:

* Start Session 2
* Start Session 3
* Start Session 4
* View Results

Dashboard sections:

1. Start / Continue Assessment
2. My Interests
3. Recommended Videos
4. Explore Careers
5. Career Roadmaps
6. Educational News
7. Related Content

Use friendly illustrations and colorful cards.

---

# JUNIOR ASSESSMENT

Create an adaptive assessment interface.

Display:
“Assessment — Session 1”

Progress:
“Question 4 of 10”

Question example:

“What type of activity sounds most interesting to you?”

Answer cards:

* Building or creating things
* Helping people
* Solving problems
* Understanding nature

The next question should visually appear to depend on the previous answer.

Show:
“Your next question is personalized based on your answer.”

Include:

* Question
* Answer choices
* Back
* Continue
* Progress indicator

Do not make it look like a boring survey.

---

# FOUR ASSESSMENT SESSIONS

Create screens representing:

Session 1
Session 2
Session 3
Session 4

Show completed sessions using checkmarks.

Example:

✓ Session 1 — Interests
✓ Session 2 — Skills & Preferences
○ Session 3 — Personality & Activities
○ Session 4 — Future Goals

Use a clear timeline/progress design.

---

# JUNIOR RESULTS

Create a result screen for a Grade 10 student.

The result should focus on educational field selection rather than directly giving only a career.

Example:

“Your Recommended Path”

“ICS / Computer Science”

Show:

Why this may suit you:

* Strong interest in technology
* Enjoys problem solving
* Likes mathematics
* Interested in computers

Then show:

“Possible Career Directions”

* Software Engineer
* AI Engineer
* Data Scientist
* Cybersecurity

Add:

“Explore Your Roadmap”

---

# EDUCATIONAL PATH RESULT

Create a visual comparison between:

FSc
ICS
I.Com

Show cards containing:

* Subjects
* Suitable interests
* Potential career directions
* Short descriptions

Highlight the recommended path without making the interface overly complicated.

---

# CAREER ROADMAP

Create a beautiful timeline.

Example career:

“Doctor”

Roadmap:

Matric
↓
FSc Pre-Medical
↓
MDCAT
↓
MBBS
↓
House Job
↓
Specialization

Another example:

“Software Engineer”

Matric
↓
ICS / FSc
↓
BS Computer Science / Software Engineering
↓
Programming & Projects
↓
Internship
↓
Software Engineer

Each stage should have:

* Icon
* Title
* Short description
* Skills/requirements

---

# SENIOR DASHBOARD — GRADE 11, 12 & BS

Create a separate professional dashboard.

Header:

“Good morning, Alex 👋”

“Your career journey, personalized by AI.”

Hero card:

“Continue Assessment”

Display progress:
“Session 2 of 4”

Main sections:

### Potential Careers

Create career cards with:

* Career name
* Match percentage
* Short explanation
* Explore button

Example:

Software Engineer
92% Match

Data Analyst
86% Match

AI Engineer
82% Match

Do NOT make the percentages look scientifically exact; present them as AI-based compatibility indicators.

### Career Analytics

Create visual charts showing:

* Interest areas
* Skill preferences
* Career categories
* Assessment trends

### Career Roadmap

Show personalized career paths.

### Interview Tips

Cards such as:

* Common interview questions
* Communication tips
* Technical preparation
* Resume tips

### Career News

Create a news section with:

* Technology
* Healthcare
* Business
* AI
* Education

---

# SENIOR ASSESSMENT

Use the same four-session structure but with more advanced questions.

The questions should explore:

* Skills
* Interests
* Academic preferences
* Career goals
* Work preferences
* Personality-related preferences
* Future goals

The questions must be adaptive.

The UI should clearly communicate:

“Your next question is based on your previous answer.”

---

# SENIOR RESULTS

Create a professional AI result dashboard.

Title:

“Your Career Insights”

Show:

Top Potential Careers

1. Software Engineer
2. Data Analyst
3. AI Engineer

For each career show:

* Compatibility indicator
* Why it matches
* Required skills
* Education
* Roadmap
* Related content

Also include:

“Explore Career”

“View Roadmap”

“Recommended Resources”

---

# VIDEO RECOMMENDATION SCREEN

Create a personalized video recommendation page.

Title:

“Recommended For You”

Categories:

* Based on your interests
* Based on your assessment
* Career skills
* Educational guidance

Each video card should contain:

* Thumbnail
* Title
* Duration
* Category
* Short description

The recommendation system will later use a recommendation algorithm.

---

# NEWS SCREEN

Create personalized career/education news.

Categories:

* Technology
* AI
* Healthcare
* Business
* Education

Use clean news cards.

---

# PROFILE SCREEN

Include:

Profile picture
Name
Education level
Interests
Assessment progress
Career interests

Options:

